+Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`. A commit range for the `yamt --diff=<range>` window (plan §2 #103–#105, #107): `lib.rs` (the IPC types `RangeFileId`, `RangeSideLabel`, `RangeSide`, `RangeChange`, `RangeLineCounts`, `RangeEntry`, `RangeStart`, `RangeEntryKind`, `RangeModeChange`, `RangeSides`, `RangeFile`; `Error`), `spec.rs` (`RangeSpec::parse`: split at the first `..`, a third dot means three dots, no further `..`, no side starting with `-`, an empty side is `HEAD`; `SpecError` carries the usage lines), `open.rs` (`Resolved::resolve`: `discover`, two `commit_named`, `merge_base` for `...`, two `commit_summary`; `Resolved::list` → `Range`: one `changed_files`, one `blob_sizes` over every side but a gitlink; `Range::start`, `Range::load`; `Range` is immutable and `Sync`), `entries.rs` (`FileAt`/`BlobAt`: rows sorted by display path, ids in that order, a deleted row named by its old path, paths lossy UTF-8 for display only), `load.rs` (`decide` from listing data in #105's order — submodule, kind change, mode only, git's numstat binary, over `yamt_merge_core::MAX_TEXT_BYTES` — so such a blob is never read; then one `BlobReader` for at most two blobs, UTF-8 per side, `Texts` with `yamt_merge_core::compare`), `lock.rs` (`PairLock`: `File::try_lock` on `<range_dir>/<repo key>/<left id>-<right id>/lock` for the process's life; repo key = the repository's folder name (the common git dir's, or its parent's when it is `.git`) + `-` + FNV-1a 64 of the absolute common git dir, so every worktree shares it). Depends on `yamt-gitio` and `yamt-merge-core` only among `yamt-*`, never on tauri (`scripts/arch-check.sh`). Tests: unit tests in `spec.rs`, `entries.rs`, `lock.rs`; `tests/range.rs` against real temp repositories (`yamt-conflict-repo`), deleting loose objects to prove what the listing answers is never read.
